SUMMARY:The Navigator — In Theatres
DESCRIPTION:Movie: The Navigator\nRuntime: 90 min\nDirector: Jordan Manley\
 nGenre: Documentary\n\nIn 1980\, Nainoa Thompson became the first Native Ha
 waiian in six centuries to navigate a voyaging canoe from Hawaii to Tahiti 
 without a compass or modern instruments. Nearly 50 years later\, he embarks
  on the demanding open-ocean crossing one final time. He and a small crew o
 f student navigators rely solely on the stars\, nature's clues and lessons 
 from the late master navigator Mau Piailug to guide them. As they sail 2\,4
 00 miles along the same sea road as their ancestors\, they bear the respons
 ibility of keeping this ancient knowledge alive. Naina sails not only to fi
 nd an island but to search for something unseen. The Navigator reveals what
  is possible when we closely observe and deeply connect with the natural wo
 rld.
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1789363
END:VEVENT
